1
00:00:00,025 --> 00:00:02,693
Soyara is an agentic DEX on GenLayer.

2
00:00:02,775 --> 00:00:07,905
AI agents trade for you, and GenLayer validators decide
whether each trade is fair.

3
00:00:07,986 --> 00:00:10,608
Here is every feature, and how to use it.

4
00:00:11,419 --> 00:00:19,219
Open AI Trading and switch the network to Studio Next,
GenLayer’s Consensus v0.6 network.

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:27,372
Studio Next has no EVM, so one Intelligent Contract,
SoyaraAgentDex, holds the balances and pools, judges each

6
00:00:27,372 --> 00:00:29,213
trade and settles it.

7
00:00:29,304 --> 00:00:33,180
Connect a wallet. The app adds the Studio Next network for
you.

8
00:00:33,261 --> 00:00:39,459
Type “get test funds”. Your agent key in this browser claims
them, so there is nothing to sign.

9
00:00:43,855 --> 00:00:52,050
You get 1,000 USDC, 1,000 USDT, 0.25 ETH and 2 WGEN, plus
GEN for fees.

10
00:00:52,138 --> 00:00:56,269
Ask for a trade in plain words. The contract quotes its own
pool.

11
00:00:56,350 --> 00:01:02,292
The card shows the price impact, your minimum, and the live
Bradbury market it will be checked against.

12
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:08,758
Press Swap and sign once. Transaction Kit quotes a small
deposit, refunded when the round is final.

13
00:01:11,151 --> 00:01:17,625
Every validator now reads the live Soyara pool on Bradbury
on its own. The trade settles only within your slippage of

14
00:01:17,625 --> 00:01:18,533
that price.

15
00:01:18,615 --> 00:01:25,672
Settled, about 0.3% under the live price, pool fee included.
The status line links the transaction.

16
00:01:25,764 --> 00:01:30,035
To let your agent trade on its own, write its limits in your
own words.

17
00:01:30,115 --> 00:01:35,152
Sign once. Validators check the per-trade cap against the
depth of the live market.

18
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:40,293
Each validator’s language model also checks that the caps
are no looser than what you wrote.

19
00:01:44,152 --> 00:01:50,675
Validators are voting. This round takes a little longer,
because every validator also asks its own model.

20
00:01:50,763 --> 00:01:54,918
The mandate is live, with its budget, per-trade cap and time
left.

21
00:01:55,002 --> 00:02:01,084
Now ask for a trade inside the mandate. Your agent settles
it in seconds, with no wallet popup.

22
00:02:08,164 --> 00:02:13,758
The contract still checks the budget, the cap, the expiry
and the price band on every trade.

23
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:18,877
A trade over the per-trade cap never goes to the agent. It
comes back to you to sign.

24
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:23,252
This order is more than 10% of the live Bradbury ETH market.

25
00:02:23,335 --> 00:02:28,488
Sign it anyway, and the validators refuse it and store the
reason. Nothing moves.

26
00:02:32,154 --> 00:02:36,866
A refusal is decided by consensus too, so it takes a normal
round.

27
00:02:40,204 --> 00:02:45,125
Refused: too large for the live market, and it tells you the
most it will take.

28
00:02:45,207 --> 00:02:51,753
The Trader Swarm puts seven agents on a trade before
anything is signed. It remembers you chose Studio Next.

29
00:02:51,836 --> 00:02:57,268
The router quotes the pool. The Market Analyst reads the
Bradbury pool the validators will read.

30
00:02:57,348 --> 00:03:03,732
The Settlement Strategist sees your mandate covers it. The
auditor checks the pool is the canonical Bradbury pair.

31
00:03:03,819 --> 00:03:10,342
Execute, and your agent settles it. The auditor confirms
your balances moved exactly as the verdict says.

32
00:03:16,702 --> 00:03:21,321
An order the validators would refuse is stopped here, before
you sign anything.

33
00:03:21,403 --> 00:03:28,112
Details shows the market read, the pre-flight checks, the
contract call and every input the contract refuses.

34
00:03:28,202 --> 00:03:33,773
Back on AI Trading, you can revoke the mandate at any time
with one signature.

35
00:03:37,515 --> 00:03:41,391
Revoking is a transaction as well, so it goes through a
round.

36
00:03:41,472 --> 00:03:43,653
Your agent can no longer trade it.

37
00:03:43,737 --> 00:03:47,775
Every trade and every refusal is a transaction on Studio
Next.

38
00:03:47,858 --> 00:03:52,639
The explorer shows its status, its fees, and how the
validators voted.

39
00:03:52,722 --> 00:03:59,361
Soyara is also a full DEX on GenLayer Bradbury. Swap routes
every trade through the aggregator’s best path.

40
00:04:03,994 --> 00:04:08,102
Pools lists every market, and it is where liquidity is added
and removed.

41
00:04:08,185 --> 00:04:11,202
Portfolio shows your balances and positions.

42
00:04:11,285 --> 00:04:17,918
On Bradbury, AI Trading settles through a Solidity
AgentExecutor that only accepts verdicts and mandates the

43
00:04:17,918 --> 00:04:20,060
AgentValidator contract wrote.

44
00:04:20,143 --> 00:04:26,597
Agent Studio lets developers run the swarm under their own
limits, and tamper with an order to watch settlement refuse

45
00:04:26,597 --> 00:04:27,061
it.

46
00:04:27,145 --> 00:04:32,739
Build Agents documents the Soyara SDK, so your own agents
can trade the same way.

47
00:04:32,821 --> 00:04:36,720
And Docs explains every part, including Studio Next.

48
00:04:37,410 --> 00:04:40,845
Soyara. Agents trade, GenLayer decides.

49
00:04:40,927 --> 00:04:43,712
Try it at app.soyara.xyz
